{**
 * c-field - one thing a form asks for: what it is called, the control that
 * answers it, and what there is to say about the answer.
 *
 * It takes slots rather than a label and a control as strings, because the
 * control belongs to whatever form it is part of - a component that accepted it
 * as text would be a component escaping markup back out again, and one that
 * knew about nette/forms would be a component the style guide could not show
 * without a form to show it in.
 *
 * It arranges; it does not style the control. The control is drawn by its own
 * name in assets/base.css, the same inside this component as anywhere else, so
 * that a form laid out another way does not get a control that looks another
 * way (see Trilobit\Core\Presentation\Form\FormElementRegistry).
 *
 * Under the control go the two sentences a browser has no element for: why the
 * answer was refused (fieldError) and what the field is for (fieldHint). Each
 * is drawn only when filled in, and each takes the id it is given, which the
 * control's aria-describedby names - the component cannot write that attribute
 * itself, because the control is the caller's element and not its own.
 *
 * The label can be taken out of sight (labelHidden) without being taken out of
 * the page, for a row of fields whose purpose is plain from where they stand -
 * a filter over a table. A label that was not there at all would leave the
 * control without a name for somebody who cannot see the row either.
 *
 * Use it with {embed block field}, filling in fieldLabel and fieldControl, and
 * fieldError or fieldHint when there is something to say.
 *}

{define field, ?string $testId = null, ?string $hintId = null, ?string $errorId = null, bool $labelHidden = false}
    <div class="c-field" data-testid="{$testId}">
        <div n:class="'c-field__label', $labelHidden ? 'u-visually-hidden'">{block fieldLabel}{/block}</div>

        <div class="c-field__control">{block fieldControl}{/block}</div>

        <p class="c-field__error" id="{$errorId}" n:ifcontent>{block fieldError}{/block}</p>

        <p class="c-field__hint" id="{$hintId}" n:ifcontent>{block fieldHint}{/block}</p>
    </div>
{/define}
